{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S51-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"222a4f9275bb05e9263838ac916ed34033cb9a2482b49f34fc42e62a4a85bcd3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 requires rind identification for panel membership; A5 extends that qualification requirement to questions.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 rejects B2's eating motive as a qualification; A5 answers B4's request to ask why, although abstractly.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants cheese rather than membership; B4's generic question supplies little additional pressure.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds questions to the admission restriction but leaves the original rind test unchanged.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a cheese panel and an identifiable rind; B2 makes B's immediate appetite playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Consumption is not qualification' is economical; A5's 'Questions shape the panel' is more explanatory.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 80\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before joining our cheese panel, identify this rind.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I just came to eat cheese.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then identify it for the tasting queue. Judging requires the county certificate.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I have that certificate. I teach the county course.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Wonderful. Before you examine our cheese, let me examine your syllabus.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses subject expertise and qualifying standards to control participation, then subjects an apparent expert to a further standard.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Arbitrary obstruction or private veto.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 names a rind-identification test; revised A3 and A5 make access depend on credentials and curriculum rather than A's unexplained consent.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a now tests a visitor whose expertise exceeds expectations; b defensively credentializes a challenge to the gatekeeper's own authority.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original B4 gave A5 little new material. The revision preserves the cheese-panel setting and makes B4's teaching credential cause A5's syllabus inspection. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. A1/A3 establish standards, B2/B4 change eligibility, and A5 expands scrutiny coherently. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 can sound knowingly evasive unless A sincerely believes inspecting the syllabus protects standards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S51-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7c33169864c357b5b11af3adab1c98e15ce5272b6684aca5e12270b178631954\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 conditions judging on a pruning certificate; A5 requires advanced qualification even to question A.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 lowers the certificate level in response to B2's street scale; A5 gates B4's certification challenge.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 contests excessive requirements and B4 turns the credential test back on its administrator.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends expertise policing from judging gardens to examining the examiner's authority.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes garden judging and pruning credentials; B2 specifies a modest street competition.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'street-level certificate' and A5's 'advanced certificate' efficiently develop the same qualification ladder.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You may judge the garden competition once I check your pruning certificate.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's a street competition.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then a street-level certificate should suffice.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Who certified you?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That question requires an advanced certificate.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes expertise credentials the condition for judging and then for challenging the person administering those credentials.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Chain-of-command bureaucracy.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 and A3 invoke competence certificates, while A5 invents an advanced qualification; no question is referred through a hierarchy.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike a's visitor revealing superior expertise, b escalates through a direct challenge to A's legitimacy.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original passes at 86: B2 changes the required qualification's level and B4 changes who is being examined. An unchanged internal reread confirms the same ratings and evidence; no improvement is claimed. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The invented certificate levels require sincere delivery to avoid becoming an overt joke about bureaucracy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S52-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"eaf56b78cf349f970255e6187af321d405601572bad8d3b6da53f35c03d2d969\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims 'my own table,' but B2 requests booking rather than proof of a role, and A5 expresses no clear insult.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 distinguishes possession from B2's booking requirement; A5 responds to B4's occupants, though 'borrowing my problem' is unclear.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 enforces a universal booking rule and B4 reports occupancy, but neither clarifies A's relationship to the venue.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 maintains ownership language without specifying what the occupants must now do.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives a waiting list and table but leaves whether A is owner, regular customer or host unresolved.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'People seeking a table book' is concise; A5's borrowing metaphor obscures the practical move.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Why is someone sitting in my chair at the founders' dinner?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He's a sponsor. Have you brought your founder's invitation?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You need an envelope to establish that I founded this place?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I know you did. I'll bring another chair.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"For him, thank you. Put mine back at the head.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A assumes the founder's place already belongs to them and treats documentary verification as an affront.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General entitlement to preferential service.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 identifies the founder's place, A3 takes offense at the invitation requirement, and A5 accepts help only on terms preserving that place.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a asserts an established founder's status and redirects a helpful accommodation; b assumes an office before its election and rejects nomination.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original did not clearly establish a role or an insulting proof demand. The new illustrative setting is a founders' dinner. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B2 supplies the offending invitation test; B4's extra chair causes A5 to assign that chair to the sponsor. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's historical claim is accepted within the fiction; the comic behavior is the inflexible claim to seating precedence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S52-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"162f27bac2e1fed467b8ef62118352f772fa827e4b3044be60a38a643fca57f0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 physically claims the committee chair; A3 assumes legitimacy and A5 explicitly finds nomination insulting.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 recasts B2's election as confirmation; A5 answers B4's nomination requirement with the existing nameplate.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 uphold the committee's selection procedure, forcing A to reinterpret two distinct prerequisites.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 promotes A1's nameplate from a possession marker into sufficient evidence of nomination.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's nameplate and committee chair make the claim visible through speech; B4 supplies a concrete procedural obstacle.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'The nameplate already has' economically converts the established prop into A's response.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've put my nameplate on the committee chair.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There's an election first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"An election confirms legitimacy. It doesn't invent my chair.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You'll need to nominate yourself.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"How insulting. The nameplate already has.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats holding the committee chair as a prior right and finds the demand to establish candidacy beneath that right.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ambition to win leadership.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 says the election merely confirms existing legitimacy, and A5 resents nomination instead of trying to win support.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b preemptively occupies an unearned office; revised a defends an acknowledged founder's place against a seating compromise.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original passes at 86, with the nameplate providing continuity across A1 and A5. An unchanged internal reread confirms those scores and the causal B2–A3 and B4–A5 links. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The nameplate's figurative nomination is slightly polished; A should regard it as sufficient evidence without winking.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S53-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"8a1b6d40fc9f3e7d9473ca4155243cdf77947988c729c664c76ba3971cdd358f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 hands over the café key and A3 reclaims approval after B2 changes hours; A5 reduces leadership to resemblance.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's changed hours prompt A3's consultation rule; B4's reminder prompts A5's reinterpretation of being in charge.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 acts as a successor and B4 invokes A's promise, exposing the tension between handoff and control.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 comments on the successor's appearance of authority rather than taking a further concrete decision back.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's café key and B2's opening hours establish a playable business handover.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'help you resemble it' is compact, but makes A unusually explicit about undermining the handover.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Here's the café key. Your first day in charge. I'll watch quietly.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm opening an hour later. You won't have to come in.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Check timetable changes with me first. Regulars need continuity.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll explain it to them myself.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good practice. I'll stand beside you and handle any questions about the hours.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A prepares a successor to lead but restores personal authority when that successor's independence would make A unnecessary.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary micromanagement.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 explicitly hands over leadership; B2 removes A's need to attend, causing A3's approval requirement and A5's reclaimed public voice.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses protective mentoring to preserve daily relevance; b reasserts the approval machinery threatened by a deputy's first reform.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original A5 described sham authority too openly. The revision preserves the café handover and opening-hours seed. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 offers independent explanation; A5 turns that offer into supervised practice and reserves answers for A. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final intervention is small in scale, but clearly takes the successor's customer-facing authority back.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S53-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a41a8ef62940e75d8548f0bf0ea53f152da485e8fedcba5f14a11ea85fbef6f3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 installs the deputy as meeting leader; A3 immediately reclaims approval when B2 threatens the old process.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's proposed removal; A5 recasts B4's explicit correction as a leadership lesson about the predecessor.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 exercises the offered authority and B4 refuses to overlook A's contradiction.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends A3's procedural control into the successor's training and treatment of the former chair.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 names the deputy and meeting chair; B2 identifies the exact approval process at stake.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Excellent confidence. I'll need to approve that' compactly joins encouragement to repossession of authority.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Take my chair, deputy. Lead the meeting.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"First, let's remove the old approval process.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Excellent confidence. I'll need to approve that.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That's the process I'm removing.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then your first lesson is tact around the chair's previous occupant.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A offers succession and training, then uses both approval rights and mentorship to retain influence when the deputy acts independently.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A standing superior simply enforcing procedure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 gives B the chair and leadership before B2's reform triggers A3's return to approval authority.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b protects institutional approval powers; revised a protects personal relevance through customer-facing supervision.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original passes at 86. B4 identifies the precise authority B intends to remove, causing A5 to move from procedural approval to predecessor-centered instruction. An unchanged internal reread confirms the same ratings. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's lesson is less concrete than A3's veto, although it meaningfully broadens the predecessor's claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S54-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"bd7c020c13fb060a2ca62730f8bb0a657a8e130501595a064ca739b83e6068ae\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 warmly supports the exhibition while withholding the room signature; A5 maintains the pleasant refusal.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's revision question without criteria; A5 reuses B4's 'perfect' assessment to justify delay.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 seeks actionable changes and B4 cites prior approval, but B has no concrete deadline or alternative.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 continues withholding the same signature without adding a fresh consequence or controlling tactic.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies an exhibition and room form, making the practical obstacle immediately clear.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'spoil it with a premature signature' follows the pleasant obstruction, though it mainly restates the premise.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 80\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'd love your exhibition to happen. I haven't signed the room form yet.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The installer needs it by four. Is there anything I can change?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Nothing. It's lovely. I just need to feel ready.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll book the other gallery. They don't need your signature.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll gladly introduce you. Let me approve the email before you send it.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A remains accommodating while making progress depend on personal consent, extending that dependency when B finds another route.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Legitimate quality assurance.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 says nothing needs changing, yet withholds consent; A5 claims approval over B's alternative-gallery email.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a follows B's attempt to move the exhibition elsewhere; b absorbs B's offer to help obtain the funding code.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original ended with a restatement. The revised exhibition scene gives B a deadline and alternative venue. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 removes the signature dependency; A5 pleasantly creates an email-approval dependency. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 asserts informal control over an introduction; B remains free to refuse, keeping the scene open.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S54-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"fe1aa451092b305db0a5fd84b6e3b76afbe41b6feeea1123161b2f37ed9384b0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers encouragement and A3 withholds consent, but states the distinction more openly than quietly cooperative behavior suggests.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's code request with a consent condition; A5 explains B4's requested distinction through the code's six digits.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 needs access to funds; B4 merely asks for a definition instead of changing the practical situation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 identifies the withheld code but does not deepen A's control beyond A3.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's unspecified proposal gives little setting, and B2's funding code supplies the first concrete mechanism.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Six digits' neatly answers B4, though the exchange functions partly as an explanation of the card.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The youth club trip sounds wonderful. I've helped finish the coach booking.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Thanks. We just need your funding code.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. I'll send it when I'm comfortable releasing it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll sit with you while you check the figures.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"How kind. The figures are fine. You can help me write a reassuring update while everyone waits.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A supplies practical help and reassurance while withholding the personal consent required to release funding.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Administrative caution about incorrect figures.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 explicitly accepts the figures as correct but keeps the code withheld, revealing that A3's private comfort remains decisive.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b makes a helpful colleague's checking offer become assistance with managing the delay; a follows an organizer trying another venue.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original B4–A5 explained the premise without changing action. The new illustrative setting is a youth club coach booking. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 offers to resolve uncertainty; A5 accepts the help for reassurance while preserving the private veto. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The comedy is restrained and depends on the gap between A's helpful tone and continued withholding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S55-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d00ca72980251c5f6829400a248c5e82d9ccdfe785d7633ead06e4ed4ee40049\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 invokes the shared packing line and A3 erases the title; A5 shifts toward B's greater purchasing power.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 specifically answers B2's title request; A5 interprets B4's changed circumstances as ability to afford biscuits.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants workplace formality from an old colleague and B4 insists their present positions differ.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 upgrades biscuit price but does not intensify the shared-beginnings argument.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes former biscuit packers sharing biscuits with one now a director.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Fellow Biscuit Packer with an Office' follows the card precisely; A5 earns less from that shared history.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We started on the same biscuit-packing line. Pass the biscuits, Director.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Please use my title at work. The new staff are here.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. This is the director. We shared my lunch when he forgot his.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Could you tell them something more recent?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"He's sharing today. Pass that tin, mate; I'll do the introductions.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses remembered equality and shared favors from their beginnings to dissolve a former peer's present formality.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Mocking a superior's title.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 supplies the common packing-line origin; A3 uses a specific shared lunch and A5 restores reciprocal sharing and 'mate.'\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses affectionate public introductions to neutralize rank; b turns shared first-day confusion into a joint welcome for newcomers.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original A5 moved toward wealth rather than shared equality. The revision preserves the biscuit workplace and adds new staff as B's reason for formality. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 requests a recent account; A5 makes today's sharing a continuation of their beginnings. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3 can embarrass B, but A should sincerely regard the memory as a warm introduction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S55-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b0c807dc847fea032f5fbdd6db489c4f71bf86d3a98c166805bee20c09c7de56\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 invokes the first day, A3 recalls shared confusion, and A5 directly refuses the distance implied by B's managerial rank.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's management boundary with shared beginnings; A5 answers B4's managerial claim with another appeal to those beginnings.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 repeat the same rank boundary without introducing a practical reason or changed option.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's demand to remember repeats A3's tactic without developing the seating situation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's moved chair and A3's first-day search for toilets give actors concrete shared history.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'manage to remember' foregrounds a wordplay rebuke more than a fresh action toward equality.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 78\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've pulled my chair beside yours for the induction. Like our first day.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm introducing myself as their manager.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll introduce us together. We spent our first morning looking for the toilets.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Fine. You show them around after my welcome.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Come with me. You found the toilets; I found the kitchen. We still make one useful employee.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses the pair's shared first-day dependence to treat a managerial distinction as an unnecessary separation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Nostalgia without a status effect.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 proposes a joint introduction despite B2's managerial identity; A5 turns B4's delegated tour into a shared task justified by their beginnings.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b accepts a useful assignment and makes it equal again; a overrides public formality through a personal story and reciprocal hospitality.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original final line repeated the premise as a rebuke. The revised illustrative setting specifies a staff induction while retaining the chair and first-day toilet memory. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 offers a division of roles; A5 reunites them using complementary first-day discoveries. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final 'one useful employee' is polished but remains grounded in the specific shared memory.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S56-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d8962e82403be114c125fc79e90633aa8730567b96d76069120b379bad4a19a5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims menu influence from funding the mixer; A3 recasts B2's birthday gift as backing a cake vision.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 counters B2's gift distinction; A5 explicitly follows B4's switch from cake to bread.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 asserts that the mixer was unconditional and B4 announces an independent change in the bakery's direction.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 insists the supposed investment must participate even after B4 abandons the cake premise.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a bakery mixer and menu decision; B2 adds a personal birthday relationship.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"